A||||37||TRiAD||My 2M4 automatic outran an F1 car!!!||||1||
Z||000000||TRiAD||09-02-2001||07:25 PM||||I don't know what this guy was doing, but he had a REAL FerrariFormula 1 car loose on the streets of Peoria!!! <P>I tracked him down at a light, and blipped the throttle. He revved back a few times, so I gave the "thumbs up"!<P>The light turned green, and we both hit it! Of course, I knew he had like 14 gears to shift through just to get to 60, so I started in 2nd, to increase my obvious advantage! After I bog down and almost stall, I get back into useful revvs, and pull away from him like he was on bricks! I guess he didn't know how to drive!<P>I hear that bumblebee fartcan torqueless rev-monster blowing his own eardrums out and busting his knuckles with every shift, while I climb the torque curve of my massive Iron Duke. I'm watching that shell of a car get smaller and smaller in my Wal*Mart special rear-view mirror, while I ready myself for the difficult shift of the automatic into 3rd. <P>My massive flying steed gallops into 3rd, hardly missing a beat, while the carbon and plastic POS behind me still shifts away, shift after shift, losing time with each change of the sequential gearbox. <P>Lucky for him, I got caught at the next light, and he caught up with me. It took him the entire red light to get his go-cart back into 1st gear, and I let him take off alone, and acted like I stalled the Pegasus-mobile. See, I knew there was a cop a mile or two down the road, since my Tech4 was getting ready to boil the readiator..it always does that right before a cop goes by, and I didn't want a ticket for drag racing. <P>So, mark up another improbable kill for the Fiero, owing solely to my apt driving ability and cool cunning under the ultimate pressure.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000001||dennis_6||09-02-2001||07:33 PM||||I hope you have an abestos suit ready.  Hell fire ready to rain from the sky!<P>P.S.  I once beat a parked corvette with a chevy corsica.  Just barely.  Might have turned out different had the car been running or had there been a driver.||||reg||4
