Z||000007||IwannaIRM||09-02-2001||10:53 PM||||Ok, let me be the first to raise the  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> flag.<P>Someones gerbils aren't running completely around the wheel and I am not talking about the engine of the 2M4.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>AIM - SWags2933<P>84 Fiero SE (being modified)<BR>88 Formula||||reg||1
Z||000008||Pontiaddict||09-03-2001||03:34 AM||||I know exactly what you are trying to do and I think it's lame. See <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/003186.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/003186.html</A>  for those who don't know what I mean.<P>How about this...<BR>I was cruisin in my good ol 84 duke when I pull to this stop light.<BR>As I stop for the light, I notice this Dodge Viper rumbling slowly to a stop. The kid driving it didn't look any older than 17, and since he had his window down, I asked, "How did a kid like you get his hands on a Viper?" He responds, "Rich dead uncle." Quite rudely I may add.<BR>So I figured that I'd show him what Duke power stood for.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>I said, "Hey, You're gonna look stupid when I take off and leave you behind."<BR>I think he got the message when he started laughing hysterically and repeatedly revved that 8 liter V10. <BR>Lights gonna change soon. So I rev the duke to 5 grand and dump the clutch when it turns green. I'm not too concerned about the 2.5, a v8's going in next week. It's a good thing too, because I must have burned through half the clutch taking off. As I shift into second, I notice that the Dodge didn't blow past me like I figured it would. So I look back in the rearview.<BR>The kid managed to do a 180 with all that horsepower, he didn't even make it into the intersection. And now he's facing a rather large truck, with an angry driver, that was behind him only moments ago. When I get my v8 installed, I'll have to remember to feather the gas when I launch. I don't want to look like a fool, getting yelled at by some angry truck driver. Then again, I just beat a Viper with an iron duke, what do I need a v8 for? <P>Now that's comedy.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Pontiaddict (edited 09-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Galen||09-03-2001||08:08 AM||||ponti, whut up G <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>you wouldn't happen to have aim would ya?<P>------------------<BR>Ray -  <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>  - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank><B>Fierolinks!</B></A><BR><FONT COLOR="purple">1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe</FONT> - <FONT SIZE="1">under construction</FONT><BR><LI> AIM<B>:</B> Fiero88cpe<FONT SIZE="1"><BR><LI> ICQ<B>:</B> 98668558</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000010||TRiAD||09-03-2001||11:05 AM||||Pontiaddict, I wasn't singling him out (ot I would have posted the link). <BR>Thanks for calling this thread lame, dumbass.<BR> <BR><B>I was simply making light of all the unrealistic "kill" stories that get posted here from time to time, not the S2000 story in particular.</B><P>Thanks for reminding me why I don't hang out here much anymore. <P>I hope the stooge that posted that S2000 story appreciates you embarrassing him in this thread now, in addition to his own. <P>L8rs. ||||reg||1
