Z||000027||TRiAD||09-05-2001||09:53 AM||||Yeah, I just made a super-secret mod on my car. Since it has the VTEC head on it now, I figured a wheel-sensor (out of my junk POS 911 GT2 out back) on the crankshaft would be a better way of making the ignition system than that crap "standard" the government makes everyone use. <BR>Everyone <I>knows</I> the government makes everyone backwards-engineer their cars to keep technology advances from making any car from 1970-on go like 200+MPH, which of course they all could otherwise. <P>So, I put this wheel sensor on the crankshaft, and made the ignition system spark from that, deleting the distributor altogether. That gave me 200% more spark energy and accuracy. <BR>Then I used the infra-red system from an optical mouse to read the position of the throttle body, and that controlls the VTEC cam timing, can control the ignition  timing, and controls when the hydrogen injection is activated.<BR>All this works with my cryo-treated pistons (I put them in the freezer at McDonald's, where I work, for a whole week!), and heat treated crank (regular oven, ALL the way up, for a whole day!), to make somewhere near 500HP (on the juice) at 14,000RPM. <BR>Yeah, it's a bad-ass design, and it's the only one like it! I outrun Vette's, Vipers, Porsches, NSXs, Diablos, Ferraris, and those POS F-bodies all day long. <BR>Yeah, no one can touch my Fiero.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
